--- !u!114 &-1741144204907423468
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '1. On the <b>Unity Asset Transformer Toolbar</b>, select the
      <b>Import Model</b> button.


      2. We provide a CAD file that you will
      use in this tutorial. In the <b>file browser window</b>, go to  <b><your project
      folder></b> > <b>Assets</b> > <b>CADModel</b> > <b>Robot</b>, there, find the
      <b>moto.SLDASM</b> and select <b>Open</b>.


      3. In the <b>Inspector</b>
      window, select <b>Import.</b>'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-1613705572162522722
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '<b>Note</b>: After import, the button will change to <b>Re-Import</b>.



      Once
      you select Import, Unity creates a new import <b>ScriptableObject</b> in your
      project. This object saves your import settings, which allows consistent re-importing.

      The
      import process is now initialized, and your <b>ScriptableObject</b> is ready
      for configuration.

'
--- !u!114 &-1469841882045615844
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '1. In the <b>Project window</b>, navigate to <b>Assets</b> >
      <b>3DModels</b>.


      2. Select the <b>Import ScriptableObject</b> created
      in the last step.


      <b>Configure model settings</b>


      3. In the
      <b>Inspector window</b>, select the <b>Model</b> tab.


      4. Ensure <b>Scale</b>
      is set to <b>0.001</b>. Unity uses meters by default, and this setting allows
      you to convert your CAD model units (millimeters in this case) to Unity meters.


      5.
      Ensure <b>Orientation</b> is set to <b>Automatic</b>. This will ensure that
      your model will use the <b>Y-up</b> system that is the Unity default.


      6.
      Ensure <b>Import Metadata</b> is enabled. The metadata will allow you to use
      all the valuable CAD information associated with the mode.


      7. Set <b>Mesh
      Quality</b> to <b>Maximum</b>.


      8. Check <b>Repair Instances</b> to
      optimize repeated geometry.


      9. Select <b>Re-Import</b> in the Inspector.'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
